{"type":"text","timestamp":1794861056648,"sessionID":"ses_e19f2b191ffe2bZOIWhJPQ0E2h","part":{"id":"prt_1e60e3c04001no6ocywyGNw0x6","messageID":"msg_1e60e364c001puVNJEm13Ub5co","sessionID":"ses_e19f2b191ffe2bZOIWhJPQ0E2h","type":"text","text":"Refactored `orders/summary.py` into 10 small functions (longest is 17 lines), keeping `summarize(orders)` as the entry point.\n\n**Structure**\n| Function | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `summarize` (summary.py:10) | Orchestrates accumulators + report |\n| `_process_order` | Per-order flow: status → items → strict skip → totals |\n| `_scan_items` | Item validation, subtotal, SKU unit counts |\n| `_discount_for` / `_tax_for` / `_shipping_for` | Coupon, tax, shipping rules |\n| `_add_customer_total` | Per-customer order count + running spend |\n| `_top_sku` / `_best_customer` | Report tie-breaking |\n| `_build_report` | Assembles the result dict |\n\n**Behaviour preserved exactly** — verified with a differential harness comparing old vs. new implementations over 25,000+ cases (edge cases + randomized), asserting identical key order, identical float bit patterns (`repr`-level), identical problem ordering, and no input mutation. Subtle quirks kept intact:\n- Valid items of a strict-skipped order still count toward `top_sku` (summary.py:30 skips *after* scanning).\n- Revenue sums per-order rounded totals, rounding only at the end; per-customer `spent` rounds after each order.\n- `top_sku` tie-break by `(-units, str(sku))`; `best_customer` keeps the first of equal spenders.\n\n`python -m unittest discover -s tests` passes (3/3); tests and `orders/` package files were not modified.","time":{"start":1794861054980,"end":1794861056644}}}
